  "id": "Compound::DB00961 - Gene::6335",
  "verbalization": "Mepivacaine is likely to interact with Scn9a through a shared mechanism involving voltage-gated sodium channels. The evidence suggests that Mepivacaine binds to Scn8a and Scn4a, both of which participate in voltage-gated sodium channel activity, and this activity is also participated by Scn9a. This implies that Mepivacaine may influence Scn9a through a common pathway involving sodium channel activity. The binding of Mepivacaine to these channels could modulate their function, potentially affecting Scn9a's role in cellular signaling. The consistent involvement of Scn9a in this process, coupled with the overlapping functional roles of Scn8a and Scn4a, supports the hypothesis that Mepivacaine exerts its effects on Scn9a via a mechanism that involves voltage-gated sodium channels. The evidence is robust and suggests a direct, mechanistic link between Mepivacaine and Scn9a through the sodium channel pathway.",
